## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses real-world Azure multi-tenant flag system design, evaluating understanding of latency optimization, tenant isolation, and change management in production environments.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags with targeting rules and environment support
- Low-latency read path with Redis caching and appropriate TTLs
- Strict per-tenant data isolation using key scoping (e.g., `flags:{tenantId}:{env}`)
- Change propagation from App Configuration to Redis via webhook triggers or event-driven updates
- Observability and auditing using Application Insights and OpenTelemetry
- Rollback/versioning strategies and experimentation/traffic splitting techniques

## Code Example

```javascript
async function getFlags(tenantId, env, userId) {
  const key = `flags:${tenantId}:${env}`;
  const cached = await redis.hGet(key, userId);
  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);

  const flags = await fetchFromAppConfig(tenantId, env);
  const userFlags = evaluateTargeting(flags, userId);
  await redis.hSet(key, userId, JSON.stringify(userFlags), { EX: 60 });
  return userFlags;
}
```

